/**
  ******************************************************************************
  * @file           : main.c
  * @brief          : TSL25911FN (TSL2591) I2C bring-up / feedback loop test
  ******************************************************************************
  * What this does (every 500 ms):
  *   1) ACK check at I2C address 0x29
  *   2) Read and print ID register (expects 0x50)
  *   3) One-time init:
  *        - ENABLE: PON + AEN
  *        - CONTROL: gain + integration time
  *   4) Wait for integration time
  *   5) Read STATUS + CH0/CH1 (0x14..0x17) and print counts
  *
  * Hardware mapping (from your schematic):
  *   - VDD = 3.3 V, GND = GND
  *   - SDA/SCL are pulled up externally (1.5k on breakout; do NOT enable internal pull-ups)
  *   - INT is pulled up (10k) but not required for this polling test
  *   - Address is fixed at 0x29
  *
  * CubeMX tips:
  *   - I2C GPIO: Alternate Function Open-Drain, Pull = No Pull
  *   - I2C speed: 100 kHz or 400 kHz (400 kHz is fine with strong pullups)
  *   - UART enabled for printf output (USART2 here)
  ******************************************************************************
  */
